### RUN .setup for group C (smtp-2026-10-23T1304): AWPTCM-T33368 SMTP server authentication.
### Cut from group B's run .setup; declares ONLY swi_d (u2, the DUT), per STANDING-ORDERS §6.
###
### This session's dispatch gives `consoles: u2 ONLY`, and this case needs no partner switch at
### all: the DUT is an SMTP *client* and the testbox is the SMTP *server*. u3 (swi_b) and u5
### (swi_a) are absent from this file entirely -- no [switch], no [baudrates], no [power], no
### [powerlink], no [boot_from_flash], no [portlink] touching them -- so the framework's
### post-failure power cycle can never reach either unit.
###
### 🔴 THIS GROUP USES eth3 <-> port1.0.10 (the vlan10 L3 underlay, DUT 10.38.22.34/27, box
###    10.38.22.33/27). That is the leg the DUT's SMTP client reaches the box over. The eth4 <->
###    port1.0.48 leg is left in group A's 802.1X rig (dot1x-controlled, no supplicant
###    authenticated, so it does NOT pass traffic) and group C does not touch it: group D
###    inherits that rig.
###
### The SMTP server is the testbox itself, two of them:
###   tools/smtpsrv.py on an UNPRIVILEGED port (>=1024), advertising AUTH PLAIN LOGIN CRAM-MD5
###   -- the instrument, logging every line the DUT sends;
###   the box's own Postfix on 0.0.0.0:25, which advertises NO AUTH -- a free negative control,
###   a real server that will not take authentication. Postfix is NOT reconfigured: adding SASL
###   to it would be a root change (STANDING-ORDERS §4).
###
### 🔴 swi_d has TWO power supplies, outlets 1 AND 8 on 10.36.230.212. The [power] stanza takes
###    ONE outlet, so a framework-initiated power cycle CANNOT actually cut this unit: the cycle
###    "completes", both PSU bays still read Ok, and only uptime shows nothing happened. A real
###    power cut needs both outlets together (`tools/tb pdu tb277 10.36.230.212 1 cycle` AND
###    `... 8 cycle`). Recorded so a silent no-op is never mistaken for a reboot.
### The box has NO deployed /home/st-art/configs/tb277.setup; never bind one.

[power]
pwr_d = (pdu, 10.36.230.212, 1)

[switch]
swi_d = /dev/u2

[baudrates]
swi_d = 115200

[stack]

[configured_stackport]

[powerlink]
swi_d = pwr_d

[boot_from_flash]
swi_d = True

[portlink]
tb-swi_d = eth3-port1.0.10, eth4-port1.0.48
